he low-rank structure of each vectorized Hankel matrix associated with the target matrix.\nL17: Our analysis reveals that for achieving exact recovery, the number of samples needs to satisfy the condition $n\\gtrsim Ksr \\log (sn)$. Empirical evaluations demonstrate the recovery capabilities and the computational efficiency of the convex method.\nL18: Subjects:  | Information Theory (cs.IT)\nL19: Cite as:  | 【12†arXiv:2401.11805】 [cs.IT]\nL20:    | (or 【13†arXiv:2401.11805v1】 [cs.IT] for this version)\nL21:    | 【14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2401.11805†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Jinchi Chen [【15†view email】]\nL25: [v1] Mon, 22 Jan 2024 10:07:52 UTC (223 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled Simultaneous Blind Demixing and Super-resolution via Vectorized Hankel Lift, by Haifeng Wang and 3 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * 【10†View PDF】\nL34:   * 【11†HTML (experimental)】\nL35:   * 【16†TeX Source】\nL36: \nL37: 【17†view license†creativecommons.org】\nL38: ### Current browse context:\nL39: \nL40: cs.IT\nL41: \nL42: 【18†< prev】   |   【19†next >】\nL43: \nL44: 【20†new】 | 【21†recent】 | 【22†2024-01】\nL45: \nL46: Change to browse by:\nL47: \nL48: 【23†cs】\nL49: 【24†math】\nL50: 【25†math.IT】\nL51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * 【26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL55:   * 【27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL56:   * 【28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (【29†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL78: \nL79: